Elegoo Connector
===============

This project contains third-party code.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
bridge/cc1client/  —  vendored from pycentauri
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

Source:  https://github.com/bjan/pycentauri
License: Apache License 2.0 (full text in bridge/cc1client/LICENSE)
Author:  bjan and pycentauri contributors

Files taken: sdcp.py, models.py, discovery.py, upload.py, mjpeg_broadcast.py,
camera.py, client.py

Changes made to the vendored code:

1. The package was renamed from `pycentauri` to `cc1client`, and intra-package
   imports were rewritten accordingly, so it cannot collide with an installed
   copy of the upstream library.
2. A minimal `__init__.py` was written for this project (upstream's `__init__`
   also exposes the CC2/MQTT client, which is not vendored here).
3. Nothing else in those files was modified. The CC2 (MQTT) client, MCP server,
   RTSP bridge, CLI and the upstream web UI were not copied.

What this code contributes: the SDCP v3 envelope and command map, the printer's
wire models and status enums, UDP discovery, the chunked multipart upload, the
single-upstream MJPEG broadcaster, and the async WebSocket client with
RequestID correlation. The protocol quirks encoded in it (5 WebSocket slots,
~60 s idle close, the dormant push scheduler, the two temperature payload
shapes) were established by that project's testing against real hardware.

